 "title": "Monroe County Ohio Tax Map Department",
 "text": "Monroe County Ohio Tax Map Department\nSkip to main content\nHome\nGovernment\nAuditor's Office\nClerk of Courts\nCommon Pleas Court\nProbate Juvenile Court\nCounty Court\nCommissioners\nBoard of Elections\nProbation Dept.\nProsecutor\nRecorder\nEngineer\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nWoodsfield P.D.\nBoard of Developmental Disabilities\nLand Bank\nDepartments\nEconomic Development\nEducation\nO.S.U. Extension\nEMA\nHealth Department\nIT Support\nJob and Family Services\nParks and Recreation\nTax Map Department\nVeteran's Office\nPublic Transportation Buckeye-Southeast Transit\nMonroe Soil and Water\nDog Warden\nMonroe County EMS Association\nFamily and Children First\nResidents\nAbout Us\nCalendar\nCounty Fair\nJob and Family Services\nLocal Businesses\nMonroe Beacon\nParks and Recreation\nChamber of Commerce\nMonroe County History\nContact Us\nCounty Directory\nCounty Email\nVisitors\nAbout Us\nContact Us\nCounty Fair\nLocal Businesses\nLodging\nMonroe Beacon\nParks and Recreation\nTourism\nRecycle Ohio\nSearch\nSearch\nslide 1 of 1\nSub Menu\nTax Map Department\nHome & About Us\nDeed Description and Survey Pre-Approvals\nGIS Hub\nParcel Viewer\nCurrent Tax Maps\nSurvey Archive\nQuarto Mining Surveys\nRailroad Surveys\nHannibal Locks & Dam Project Files\nCemetery Plats\nPlat Books\nPlat Books & Road Records\nCurrent County Highway Map\nDocuments and Files\nHistorical Maps\nLocal Surveyors List\nRoad Information\nUSGS Topo Maps\nEngineer's Office\nFAQ\nHome\nDepartments\nTax Map Department\nHome\nWelcome to the Monroe County Ohio Tax Map Department!\nOffice Hours: 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. Monday - Friday\nMap Dept. Phone: (740) 472-0763\nE-mail: mcmapdept@monroecountyohio.com\nFollow us on:\nOffice Personnel:\nTim Lumbatis Tax Map Office Supervisor\nZach Matz Deputy Tax Map Technician\nAnnouncements:\nThis office will be closed for lunch on Friday, August 14th and Monday, August 17th due to limited staff. We apologize for any inconvienance.\nAbout Us:\nThe Monroe County Tax Map Department is responsible for the creation, maintenance, and updating of a comprehensive array of resources, including GIS data, online mapping, historic maps, and survey plats. Our office diligently reviews deed descriptions during the recording process to ensure compliance with the Monroe County Requirements for Conveyance and Monroe County Subdivision Regulations, both of which are accessible on our Documents and Files page.\nTo facilitate a seamless transfer process, we offer pre-approval services for legal descriptions scheduled for future conveyance. For optimal efficiency, we recommend submitting instruments at least two days prior to the transfer date. Pre-approving all conveyance documents is highly advised to expedite the process. Submissions may be sent via mail or email, and our team strives to review legal descriptions in the order received, typically providing feedback within 24 hours. Please allow additional time for larger or more complex documents to ensure a thorough review.\nOur commitment to providing accurate and current mapping is unwavering. As we continuously update our records and correct identified errors, we encourage the public to report any discrepancies or concerns. Your input is invaluable in helping us maintain the highest standards of accuracy. Our team will investigate each reported issue and take appropriate action to enhance the reliability of our data in service to the community.\nThe Monroe County Tax Map Department is located in Room 24 on the second floor of the Monroe County Courthouse. We welcome your inquiries and visits as we work to serve you effectively.\nShare\nShare this page\nShare this page\n×\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.monroecountyohio.net/departments/tax_map_department/index.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\nMonday - Friday\n8:00 AM - 4:00 PM\nView Directory\nRoom 101 N. Main St. R34\n|\nWoodsfield, Ohio 43793\nP: +1 (740) 472-1341\nPowered by revize., the Government Website Experts Login\nClose\nRead More",
